TLS certificate for this server

The installer creates a self-signed certificate here:
  sentora.crt   certificate (public)
  sentora.key   private key (root only)

Apache (the panel and webmail), Postfix (ports 25, 465, 587) and Dovecot
(IMAP, POP3, ManageSieve) all use these two files.

To use a trusted certificate later (Let's Encrypt or your own company CA),
replace both files with the new certificate (full chain) and key, keep the
names, then run:
  chmod 600 sentora.key
  systemctl reload apache2 postfix dovecot
